<title>NETHERLANDS: PAYS-BAS PROP 9-MONTHS RESULT SHARPLY UP.</title>
<headline>PAYS-BAS PROP 9-MONTHS RESULT SHARPLY UP.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to Sept 30, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net direct investment result    13.5  vs   7.2</p>
<p>    Net rental income		   28.6  vs  23.0</p>
<p>    Interest charges		    11.5  vs  11.8</p>
<p>    Operating costs			3.7  vs   4.0</p>
<p>    Net asset value per shr (gldrs)  6.39 vs   6.06</p>
<p>NOTE - Pays-Bas Property Fund NV maintained its forecast</p>
<p>that the 1996 full-year direct investment result would be</p>
<p>considerably higher than last year's. In 1995 it posted a</p>
<p>full-year net profit of 10.9 million guilders.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
